Z||000010||falconhulk||10-10-2001||11:13 AM||||slammed is that a joke?  Not sure.  That v12 is actually one of the most advanced engines ever made.  It has the capability to shut down to just 4 cy!  MPG is going to be way up there in what ever car they put it in.  If it works like its suppose to the other 8 cyl are just a foot stomp away!!  That thing looks a lot like the new vanquish or ferri.  Did anyone else see the new mid engine car from sweden?  its in the new car and driver but they never said what it was called unless they were serious about "egg".  The body is made from 3 pieces of kevlar composite.  I looks similar to a lambo but much cooler.  Its suppose to be a contender for the production car land speed recor of 245 mph.  Its built to contend with the Mclaren F1 and costs $300,000.  BTW the roof pulls off and stores under the hood also.  This car is a monster with a 6 speed and does 100mph in 3rd!||||reg||1
Z||000011||Slammed Fiero||10-10-2001||11:50 AM||||The cimmaron thing is a joke. The fact that GM teases the public with the good stuff then slips a different thing into showrooms is not.<P>Wow... it runs on 4cyl , then 8 is just a foot stomp away. Am I the only one who remembers the 4/6/8 caddies of the early 80's? These motors were crap. This is an avenue they have been down before. I have a soft spot in my heart for caddies , I have had a 79 2 door with a big block for about 10 years now. I love it.  They need to build another rear drive caddy. My old 79 will run 120mph all day long (no joke) Lets get rid of all these FWD luxury cars. The Evoq is a step in the right direction. But look at the market, crazy over Boxsters , S2000's ect ect. if they were smart they would make the evoq retail at about 35 to 40 grand , Build a nice customer base then jack the price.<P>anyone remember when the first lexus's hit the shores? These were selling for less than an STS at the time...and I mean the original STS with the 4.9. Then once Lexus got a following the price creeped up and no one said anything.<P>I can almost predict the magazine reviews for a "sports" based caddy.<P>Whats hot:<BR>Look at me styling<BR>Power<P>Whats not:<BR>Defense department price<BR>Mushy suspension<P>Then they will go on to say that for their XXX amount of dollars they would buy a ....fill in the blank. Mercedes SLK compressor , BMW Z3 , Corvette , Boxster ..ect..ect.  Remember the allante?? Great car , espically with a Northstar they were turning mid 6's to 60 , top down , pinninfarina italian made body. The styling reflected the times , a little square. All in all every report I read about it said it was a great car , the price is what killed it.<P>Just my 2 cents.<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000012||DKOV||10-10-2001||11:51 AM||||--Actual conversation of a GM exec--<P>"Hmmm... a Northstar engine in a mid-engine GM frame...  Hmmmm...  That's never been done before!  Hey Joe, what kind of mid-engine frame do we have laying around?  A Fiero?  What the heck is that?!?!"<P>"Doesn't matter, what if we put a Nothstar engine in one?  That's never been done before...  What?  It has?  Oh, just a bunch of Kit Car guys... That's doesn't count."<P>"Just the same, maybe we should put a different body on it just in case.  Oh, and maybe beef up the horsepower to make it seem bigger that it really will be if we ever build the darn thing."<P>"After all, my next pay raise is only based on CONCEPT, right Joe!  HA HA Ha ha ha..."<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>DKOV -||||reg||1
