Z||000016||Raydar||10-10-2001||02:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tigger:<BR><B>I believe there is hope in the 4/6/8 displacement on demand setup.  It's a sensible idea being re-invented and improved with new technology.<P>Remember, a lot of engine developement has happened since the late '70s.<P>*strikes a Saturday Night Fever Pose*</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The Northstar has the capability of getting you home even if it has <I>no</I> coolant. <BR>If I understand this correctly, it does this by running on four cylinders, then it switches and runs on *the other* four cylinders. Every other rev is used to pull cool air through the cylinder, instead of making power. <BR>I believe the new system will work just fine. The old 8-6-4 system used solenoids and God-knows-what-else. Mostly mechanical stuff. <BR>Technology has advanced tremendously.<BR>Better living through electronics!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>*Stayin' alive. Stayin' alive...*<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
